  "result": "Excellent! Payment terms are now fully implemented and tested. Here's what was added:\n\n**New functionality:**\n\n1. **`src/dates.js`** \u2014 Added `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`:\n   - Calculates due dates based on three terms options:\n     - **NET14**: Due 14 days after issue date\n     - **NET30**: Due 30 days after issue date\n     - **EOM**: Due on the last day of the issue date's month\n   - Handles month and year boundaries, including leap years\n\n2. **Updated `src/invoices.js`**:\n   - `createInvoice()` now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the invoice\n   - Validates terms against the three allowed values\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n\n3. **Updated `src/errors.js`**:\n   - Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code\n\n4. **Comprehensive tests** (19 new tests in `test/invoices.test.js` and 10 in `test/dates.test.js`):\n   - Default NET30 behavior\n   - All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n   - Edge cases: leap years, month/year boundaries, end-of-month dates\n   - Invalid terms rejection\n   - Terms preservation through issueInvoice\n\nAll 187 tests pass. The feature handles edge cases like EOM in February during leap and non-leap years, and correctly calculates dates when NET14/NET30 cross month boundaries.",
